/2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-xz{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} & =-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}) & =-x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2})\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int x{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-{x}^{2}/2} & ={e}^{-{x}^{2}/2}+C \\\\ z & =1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{1+C{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse intervals where $1+Ce^{x^2/2}\\ne0$. The original equation also admits $y=0$; it is outside the requested nonzero family." 13194139542481 17592186576411 true] [17592186244217 1071 "Find the general nonzero real solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{-4}.\n$$" 13194139542481 17592186576411 true] [17592186244217 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{-4}.\n$$" 13194139542481 17592186576411 false] [17592186244217 1074 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-3{x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{2},\\,n=-4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{4}\\frac{dy}{dx}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{5}={x}^{2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5{y}^{4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}z={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThis 